/*  Regions — `Pull a rabbit` and the rule that keeps one sound: `CheckPullRabbit`,
    `CheckRegionStore`, `ValueDepthOf` and `ContainerDepthOf` in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Rabbit.cs`.

    ★ A region is a depth. Pulling a rabbit goes one deeper, a name remembers the depth it was made
    at, and a value may not be stored anywhere that outlives it — somewhere shallower.

    ★ What a CALL or a member read gives back is as deep as its signature says — see
    `region-depths.cufe`, which works that out once each function's body has been checked.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// What a series, a map, an object — anything held by reference — is; a value-typed one copies.
    Bind fact to is-reference-type, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        Return kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "MapType" or kind is "ObjectType" or kind is "MatrixType"
            or kind is "ChannelType" or kind is "AddressType".
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-rabbit-type, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is not "ObjectType", return false.
        Return (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)) in lowercase) is "rabbit".
    Done.

    /// How deep a captured parameter is taken to be: deeper than anything, so it is stored nowhere.
    Bind number to captured-parameter-depth:
        Return 2147483647.
    Done.

    /// The depth of the container being written into — its name's, or where the write stands.
    Bind number to container-depth unto checker, given (the node target):
        If target's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1))).
            If found is not void, return found's depth.
        Done.
        Return one's rabbit-depth.
    Done.

    /// A value stored where it would outlive its region is refused.
    Bind void or failure to check-region-store unto checker, given (the node value, the node value-type,
            the number target-depth, the number at-row, the text action):
        If cast is-reference-type on (value-type) is false, return.
        Define value-depth as cast one's depth-of-value on (value, value-type).
        If value-depth is greater than target-depth:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "this value lives in a shorter-lived region than its destination — it will be gone when that region ends", "",
                at-row, action,
                "Declare the container inside that region too, so both end at its 'Done.', or make the value before the region opens, so it lives as long as the container.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `Pull a rabbit [as <name>].` — one region deeper for the length of the block.
    Bind void or failure to check-pull-rabbit unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Increment one's rabbit-depth by 1.
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (named).
            Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
                the shape cast object-type-named on ("rabbit"),
                the established-by cast placed-reference on (name, at-row, cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4))),
                the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth one's rabbit-depth, the parameter false }).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
        Decrement one's rabbit-depth by 1.
    Done.
Done.
